# Bug #4855: served text files keep LF in every checkout. On Windows core.autocrlf turned robots.txt into CRLF, so the
# file served (and the image deploy.ps1 builds from that tree) differed from the one in git.
public/robots.txt text eol=lf

# AB#374 (Lander, the merge queue): append-only logs merge by keeping both sides, so a rebase onto main does not stop
# on two branches that each added a line. Local git honours this; Azure DevOps's own merge does not (tested
# 2026-10-01), which is why Lander rebases a PR itself before it lets Azure DevOps complete it.
PROGRESS.md merge=union
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
